<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Linggabuana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1357">1357</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Prabu Maharaja Linggabuana</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Linggabuana was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunda-strait">Sunda</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> from about 1350 to 1357. He travelled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a> with his daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dyah-pitaloka">Dyah Pitaloka</a> for her marriage to King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hayam-wuruk">Hayam Wuruk</a>, but was killed with his followers in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bubat">Battle of Bubat</a> after refusing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gajah-mada">Gajah Mada</a>'s demand that she be offered as tribute. Sundanese tradition remembers him as Prabu Wangi, the fragrant king.</p></div>
